WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.116
A normalized operational database and an analytical

00:00:03.142 --> 00:00:08.310
model solve different problems OLTP systems focus

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:12.313
on safe day-to-day transactions They reduce
duplicated

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:14.813
facts protect updates and use keys and

00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:20.015
constraints to preserve integrity Analytical models
focus

00:00:20.041 --> 00:00:24.320
on understandable efficient reporting Fact tables
store

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:28.004
measurable events while dimensions provide
descriptive context

00:00:29.755 --> 00:00:31.952
That means a star schema may intentionally

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.163
repeat some descriptive values in ways an

00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:38.567
operational schema would avoid The important point

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.291
is that dimensional modeling complements the
normalized

00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:44.872
source It does not excuse poor operational

00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:49.425
design A trustworthy analytical model is easier

00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:51.004
to build when the source system has

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.925
clear grain reliable identifiers controlled
relationships and

00:00:54.951 --> 00:00:56.412
well-enforced business rules
